From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: s5k4h7: Fix mode changes and system sleep while
 powered

The sensor stays powered for the autosuspend delay after streaming
stops. A format change in that window, which is when a camera stack
reconfigures, changes HBLANK between the 3264 and the 1632 pixel wide
modes. The control core calls s_ctrl for read-only controls too, and
s_ctrl rejected HBLANK with -EINVAL: set_fmt failed with the mode
already switched and HBLANK and the VBLANK range left at the old mode's
values, which a later set_fmt for the same size did not correct. Accept
the read-only controls in s_ctrl, which have no register of their own.

Refuse active format changes while streaming, which would otherwise
rewrite the frame length of the running mode.

Only runtime PM callbacks were set, so a system suspend within the
autosuspend delay left the sensor powered through the sleep, with its
supplies and MCLK on. Use DEFINE_RUNTIME_DEV_PM_OPS, which forces the
runtime suspend on system sleep.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/media/i2c/s5k4h7.c | 19 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/s5k4h7.c b/drivers/media/i2c/s5k4h7.c
index fa811ee46c..ffba28affd 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5k4h7.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5k4h7.c
@@ -422,6 +422,14 @@ static int s5k4h7_set_ctrl(struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl)
 					     ctrl_handler);
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * LINK_FREQ, HBLANK and PIXEL_RATE follow the mode and have no
+	 * register of their own; set_fmt changes them while the sensor may
+	 * still be powered.
+	 */
+	if (ctrl->flags & V4L2_CTRL_FLAG_READ_ONLY)
+		return 0;
+
 	if (ctrl->id == V4L2_CID_VBLANK)
 		s5k4h7_update_exposure_range(s5k4h7, ctrl->val);
 
@@ -634,6 +642,10 @@ static int s5k4h7_set_pad_format(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 	s64 hblank, vblank;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (fmt->which == V4L2_SUBDEV_FORMAT_ACTIVE &&
+	    v4l2_subdev_is_streaming(sd))
+		return -EBUSY;
+
 	mode = v4l2_find_nearest_size(s5k4h7_modes, ARRAY_SIZE(s5k4h7_modes),
 				      width, height, fmt->format.width,
 				      fmt->format.height);
@@ -1082,9 +1094,8 @@ static void s5k4h7_remove(struct i2c_client *client)
 	}
 }
 
-static const struct dev_pm_ops s5k4h7_pm_ops = {
-	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(s5k4h7_power_off, s5k4h7_power_on, NULL)
-};
+static DEFINE_RUNTIME_DEV_PM_OPS(s5k4h7_pm_ops, s5k4h7_power_off,
+				 s5k4h7_power_on, NULL);
 
 static const struct of_device_id s5k4h7_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "samsung,s5k4h7" },
@@ -1095,7 +1106,7 @@ MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, s5k4h7_of_match);
 static struct i2c_driver s5k4h7_i2c_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "s5k4h7",
-		.pm = &s5k4h7_pm_ops,
+		.pm = pm_ptr(&s5k4h7_pm_ops),
 		.of_match_table = s5k4h7_of_match,
 	},
 	.probe = s5k4h7_probe,
